  "notes": "Bounds finite bus-0 ordinary I2C read event waits to the remaining caller tick budget. The pinned SDK stays untouched: only the I2C object in a verified build-local archive redirects its queue receive through a task-owned deadline adapter; unrelated queues, other buses and unbounded calls retain their behavior. All 33 focused host suites, fresh independent review, the normal PlatformIO build and actual ELF/map call-chain audit passed. USB installation, normal startup, connected Twin Button and unchanged 64-row flashlight learning data were verified. Actual one-byte and 12-byte ESP_ERR_TIMEOUT reads completed in 8.118 ms and 8.003 ms instead of approximately one second, followed by fresh CRT sampling. This corrects the observed excessive wait; the underlying missed-event cause and primary IR absence are not claimed resolved. Existing sensor fault policies and other hardware fault reports remain intact.",
